An excelent short graphic novel with multiple endings and the inifinite simulacrum loop used in a post apocaliptic scenario to make a fictional moral test of the player (one wich the protagonist undoubtly fails or balances on sudden extremes)  is in a very morbid setting, allthou it is very well written(and has a notable degree of tehnical repetetive dialog pop ups) the theme is horrifying not to mention the worse setting of the way  achivments are constructed for the game.- It reminded me of adventure typing games on old computers.
Thumbs up for the literal effort to make this darkest of the dark horor fantasy ( i dont like horor at all) and for the "Sin City Frame" for the graphic novel i especially apriciate the fact that the game is totaly free without the lure of microtransactions or paywall setbacks during gameplay. It is actually very interesting but the story is rather depressing and horific and suffers from a light treatment of horrible scenarios which even makes the comic relief chat rabbit's humor distasteful. Of course dark fantasy and SF is hardly successful without these elements-unfortunately. Allthou this game should in no case be taken seriously other than a literal work of art and a good and fun game that really ingages your fantasy and intelect. I especially like that the right choises in this game are visible and kinda sugested and that they are allways the most inteligent and humane choise offered at the same time.
;-}
